{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560756-dominate-yourself","id":560756,"title":"Dominate yourself","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-19T06:47:49-07:00","id":560756,"title":"Dominate yourself","content":"Hi everyone! (I have so many inquiries lately!)<br /> <br /> I was talking to a friend who plays/runs a LARP and I am questioning on of the things that he said goes on there. I'm simply curious as to if it would be possible without house rules. They still run with 1E but I do know that they have altered some of the rules (main on I remember is that Nos no longer have that social stigma of not re-rolling 10's and 1's subtract successes. Can't remember what it was replaced with though)<br /> <br /> It's a fairly large group and has been running for the better part of a decade if not more (he's only been apart of it for the past 1-2 years). He mentioned that they have been using a bit of a work-around protection against Dominate. Which is that you, or someone you trust, Dominates you against being Dominated. I can't remember the exact details if it was either you can't be Dominated or you simply attack any vampire, other than initial user/yourself, who tries to use Dominate on you. My question is, can that actually work? Would you know if someone is trying to use it on you? Would you have enough to to react if it was simply to attack the caster, or could it be blocked out all together? (Usually eye contact is needed, so as soon as someone tries it, they break eye contact and leave the room or something)<br /> <br /> TL;DR Question: Can you use Dominate in some way to protect yourself against Dominate? Or any other mind altering Discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:54:17-07:00","id":560777,"title":"","content":"There's a devotion in the Carthians book that adds your Dominate dots to your resistance trait vs it. There's one for Nightmare and Majesty too. They all require one dot of Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:15:23-07:00","id":560787,"title":"","content":"Hi Elfive.<br /> <br /> Thanks. So there is no way to use Condition on yourself (still talking 1E, can't remember dominate in 2E) to the point where if your Beast feels the effect of another's Dominate, it freaks out? (I thought it was a nifty work around if it can actually work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:35:59-07:00","id":560808,"title":"","content":"Well, it wouldn't be as simple of just using dominate whilst looking in a mirror. However, there <i>is</i> a 2e devotion called Chain of Command that lets you implant a use of Dominate in someone else to be triggered at some other time. There's nothing stopping you from using that triggered effect on yourself. I think it would be easy enough to port back into first edition. It requires Dominate 3 and Vigor 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:00:58-07:00","id":560843,"title":"","content":"Interesting.. You could protect yourself against a wide variety of things that way.. I wonder why it never occurred to me to try that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:12:27-07:00","id":560855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560756-dominate-yourself?p=560843#post560843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.. You could protect yourself against a wide variety of things that way.. I wonder why it never occurred to me to try that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Devotion is not really practical, as in, you can only protect yourself from stuff you know yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:20:36-07:00","id":560862,"title":"","content":"Oh wait, I think I remember something. If you have been dominated by a very old/powerful vampire, say Dominate 4-5. Anything lower than that has issues overwriting that correct? So a vampire with Dominate 1-3 wouldn't be able to, or at least find it very difficult, to use his discipline on someone under that situation. Or maybe that was just a house rule.. Not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:29:54-07:00","id":560902,"title":"","content":"1e Conditioning gives the victim a penalty to resist the user's Dominate and a bonus to resist anyone else's. At maximum it can get up to +5/-5. You can't do it to yourself, but in theory you could get someone else you trust to to do it to you. The problem is you're then willingly letting someone turn you into their mind slave and just kind of hoping they won't abuse that power. Also by the fluff your character basically becomes a vegetable with no personality under the effects of heavy Conditioning. I remember the MET rules had a sidebar about doing more of a manturan candidate thing, since roleplaying a zombie would obviously not work very well in LARP. But even if your personality is apparently left intact, a character under the full effects of Conditioning is barely sentient, their free will has been all but completely supplanted by their master's commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-19-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:37:44-07:00","id":560905,"title":"","content":"The trick is to replace your own personality with an exact replica of your personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:47:28-07:00","id":560933,"title":"","content":"Hmm, interesting. It might not of been Conditioning, this was a convo from awhile ago. But ya, I'm guessing it would be something you would want to do with someone you have a blood bond with. Would be interesting to play around with though. I wonder if there could be some sort of devotion, Dominate and Auspex (would probably need to be level 4), that makes it so whenever subject is attacked or threatened/feels threatened, someone else is using Dominate (and the subject knows), he automatically tries to contact the user of the devotion to let him/her know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:32:46-07:00","id":561115,"title":"","content":"1st edition you could only be subject to one Mesmerize effect at a time. The trick is to get someone to use Mesmerize to place a benign command on you that takes effect with a predetermined trigger. (ie. Call me 15 minutes before the next sunrise.) So, If anyone else tries to Mesmerize you while the first effect is still in place, the second Mesmerize command doesn't take hold. It does rely on you trusting someone else to use Dominate on you and not insert other instructions or alter your memory further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-19-2015, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:42:41-07:00","id":563622,"title":"","content":"Dominate works by imposing your will on the subject's. Mesmerism causes their mind to turn passive and submissive while you fill the vacuum with your own thoughts and desires. There's no way to do that to yourself, as a mesmerized person lacks the initiative to muster the force of will necessary to implant commands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:11:37-07:00","id":563640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560756-dominate-yourself?p=561115#post561115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st edition you could only be subject to one Mesmerize effect at a time. The trick is to get someone to use Mesmerize to place a benign command on you that takes effect with a predetermined trigger. (ie. Call me 15 minutes before the next sunrise.) So, If anyone else tries to Mesmerize you while the first effect is still in place, the second Mesmerize command doesn't take hold. It does rely on you trusting someone else to use Dominate on you and not insert other instructions or alter your memory further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't someone else Mesmerizing you just cause a Clash of Wills, then? I mean, granted, that does give you some measure of protection, but it's far from foolproof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:46:25-07:00","id":564508,"title":"","content":"If you could dominate yourself, there are so many other tricks you could pull as well (let's say that even if you can't just look in a mirror and do it, you've got a devotion that lets you dominate yourself or something. Thought exercise time)<br /> <br /> *Establish trustworthiness. Before a business deal, diplomatic meeting or other situation where you want to form an honest alliance and want to be trusted, just publicly Dominate yourself &quot;Deal honestly and tell anyone if you plan to betray them&quot;. Suddenly, people can trust you a lot easier and you can achieve your goal without worrying about other people mistrusting you<br /> *Willpower replacement (concept, not mechanical benefit). &quot;Refuse all bribes&quot;, &quot;Quit smoking&quot; (not useful for a vampire, but just an example), &quot;Do everything in your power to kill the Prince, even what you would have considered unthinkable&quot;<br /> *Imprint reflexes. &quot;Draw your weapon the moment you think you're in danger&quot; &quot;Attack Josephine whenever you see her&quot;<br /> *Time-delayed knowledge. I forget, can you make someone forget something with dominate? If so, write a message to yourself and hide it on your person (say a little used pocket). Then, implant a command in yourself to pull the paper out of that pocket in X time and read it. Finally, remove the knowledge of the paper from your mind. With email, this gets even easier. This means that you can do tricky plans against people who can read minds or detect lies<br /> *Related to the first point, but it can be used to make contracts binding. Make it known that whenever you sign a contract, you will willingly Dominate yourself to carry it out faithfully<br /> <br /> Sure, none of these are going to provide you with mechanical benefits (except maybe the reflexes one. Depends on the ST there) but it's some cool story tools to play around with<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:44:45-07:00","id":565347,"title":"","content":"That's one of the things I was getting at. If it was possible, what else could be done? Little tricks to make traversing the political war that much safer. I understand why they didn't allow this ability, but, except for preventing yourself from being Dominated by someone else (or at least making it difficult) I don't see too much benefit other than maybe the reflex one as well. Well, unless you're character has issues telling the truth, then your first example would be wonderful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:46:50-07:00","id":565348,"title":"","content":"You do not need a supernatural power to be Trustworthy. You can, you know, just be trustworthy. Same with your Bribes example and your Contracts example... You can just refuse the bribe and honor the contract. Simple as that. Why do you need a supernatural Power to not be a douche?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:40:26-07:00","id":565395,"title":"","content":"What if being trustworthy/not being a douche goes against everything your character stands for? (for those more silly games)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:50:02-07:00","id":565406,"title":"","content":"As a character, you earn the reputation you deserve. If your goal is to be trusted, then you work towards that goal. Personal Supernatural reinforcement is ludicrous if you are not wanting to be trustworthy in the first place. You either are trustworthy (in which case you do not need the supernatural to reinforce it) or you are not (in which case the supernatural reinforcement will not matter as you are not trustworthy to begin with). If, as in your words, being trustworthy is not in your nature (against everything a character stands for), do you really think an attempt at creating such a thing will even work? I don't.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it a different way... If being trustworthy is against everything your character stands for, why would you try to use the Supernatural to be trustworthy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-23-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:39:32-07:00","id":565444,"title":"","content":"Well, like someone else wrote, it's all just food for thought. The reason that I could see for someone using the Supernatural to be trustworthy, still under the assumption that the character has no impulse control and is unable to act trustworthy, is because he needs to act so to his superiors. If you don't, then you won't get ahead. If you aren't, then you might find yourself on the tip of someone else's knife. Otherwise, I completely agree, under normal circumstances, just not act like a douche. <br /> <br /> An example of a character who might need this, I once played a chronicle with someone who was a compulsive liar. Couldn't help it. Was written into the background as someway to cope with something that happened way before the embrace. So even if he wanted to say, &quot;Yes, I understand. I'm not going to go to the Prince with this authority&quot;. It would come at as either, &quot;No, I don't get it. I won't go ...&quot; , or &quot;Yes, I understand. I'll get this information to the Prince right away!&quot;. He wouldn't actually do it, just, basically sounding like a little sarcastic muffin. <br /> <br /> But like I said, it's just food for thought. Kind of wondering what the limitations are in certain things. (originally was brought up by someone else, although I'm certain he said it was a house rule)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:44:00-07:00","id":565447,"title":"","content":"No worries, it is just a very odd premise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:52:51-07:00","id":565450,"title":"","content":"That it is. But I find that it is with the strange that things get interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T09:26:58-07:00","id":565484,"title":"","content":"Or completely over the top, depending upon ones point of view. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T11:22:01-07:00","id":565590,"title":"","content":"I like examinations of metaphysics as much as anyone.<br /> <br /> I do have to call shenanigans on Dominating yourself making you more trustworthy.<br /> <br /> Dominate is not an obvious power. You could just start into any mirror and say &quot;I totally will not betray you&quot; and nobody witnessing it would know whether or not you actually did it.<br /> <br /> I guess they could use Auspex 4 to read your mind, but I don't suspect that to be a terribly common level of Discipline to manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T08:11:23-07:00","id":566420,"title":"","content":"That's what I thought when I first heard it! If one could do that, what would be the limits! <br /> <br /> Alas, shall just have to find someone you trust dearly. Or somehow trick yourself so you don't think you are using it on yourself! Technicality? Ponders...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:47:13-07:00","id":568679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaintedPhysician</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560756-dominate-yourself?p=564508#post564508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could dominate yourself, there are so many other tricks you could pull as well (let's say that even if you can't just look in a mirror and do it, you've got a devotion that lets you dominate yourself or something. Thought exercise time)<br /> <br /> *Establish trustworthiness. Before a business deal, diplomatic meeting or other situation where you want to form an honest alliance and want to be trusted, just publicly Dominate yourself &quot;Deal honestly and tell anyone if you plan to betray them&quot;. Suddenly, people can trust you a lot easier and you can achieve your goal without worrying about other people mistrusting you<br /> *Willpower replacement (concept, not mechanical benefit). &quot;Refuse all bribes&quot;, &quot;Quit smoking&quot; (not useful for a vampire, but just an example), &quot;Do everything in your power to kill the Prince, even what you would have considered unthinkable&quot;<br /> *Imprint reflexes. &quot;Draw your weapon the moment you think you're in danger&quot; &quot;Attack Josephine whenever you see her&quot;<br /> *Time-delayed knowledge. I forget, can you make someone forget something with dominate? If so, write a message to yourself and hide it on your person (say a little used pocket). Then, implant a command in yourself to pull the paper out of that pocket in X time and read it. Finally, remove the knowledge of the paper from your mind. With email, this gets even easier. This means that you can do tricky plans against people who can read minds or detect lies<br /> *Related to the first point, but it can be used to make contracts binding. Make it known that whenever you sign a contract, you will willingly Dominate yourself to carry it out faithfully<br /> <br /> Sure, none of these are going to provide you with mechanical benefits (except maybe the reflexes one. Depends on the ST there) but it's some cool story tools to play around with</div> </div> </div> </div>A bloodline of Venture tied around the theme of self-control that slowly worked upon themselves until they were perfect sounds awesome. Clan weakness would have to be tied to either perfectionism or the unstable mind one would have after such nudging. Perhaps they must be open-minded to get it to work, hence why it isn't common among Venture and as such the clan weakness is that they are all gullible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Also, with regards to trustworthiness, publicly signally trustworthiness is an effective strategy. Just as Maina said however, I don't anyone would believe the dom-thyself signal. The general thrust though, of devastating your options to reinforce your commitment to one path (denouncing the Lance to secure oneself with the Circle, for example) is sound and is alive in the dom-thyself example. I just think it is something you'd have to allow your allies to do to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":". 06-25-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:23:03-07:00","id":569182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560756-dominate-yourself?p=568679#post568679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bloodline of Venture tied around the theme of self-control that slowly worked upon themselves until they were perfect sounds awesome</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Sotoha with Kamen, Invictus p170.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:26:22-07:00","id":569184,"title":"","content":"That does seem like an interesting bloodline. Self perfection!<br /> <br /> MCN, I shall have to take a look at this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"tha